From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:40:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/20] media: apple: vxd: size the bitstream buffer from the coded
 size

GStreamer's v4l2codecs leaves sizeimage to the driver and refuses an
access unit that does not fit.  The OUTPUT sizeimage is now at least
one byte per pixel (page aligned, still at least 1 MiB): about 2 MiB for
1920x1088, enough for a level 4.2 intra picture.

Signed-off-by: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <maintainer@example.invalid>
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-v4l2.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-v4l2.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-v4l2.c
index 9a348ff862f83b57bd209c1f767691b4c081cdef..622fb1f96788a94faf2e5d57546b2b0aad571124 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-v4l2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/vxd/apple-vxd-v4l2.c
@@ -327,8 +327,15 @@ static int apple_vxd_do_try_output_fmt(struct apple_vxd_ctx *ctx,
 			return ret;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * One access unit per buffer (frame-based decode): one byte per
+	 * pixel covers a level 4.2 1080p intra picture (about 2 MiB),
+	 * userspace such as GStreamer leaves sizeimage to the driver.
+	 */
 	pix_mp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage =
-		max(pix_mp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage, APPLE_VXD_MIN_BITSTREAM_SIZE);
+		max3(pix_mp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage,
+		     (u32)APPLE_VXD_MIN_BITSTREAM_SIZE,
+		     (u32)PAGE_ALIGN(pix_mp->width * pix_mp->height));
 	return 0;
 }
 
